Ring Topology
Definition

Each device is connected to exactly two other devices, forming a closed loo=
p (ring).

Data travels in one direction (unidirectional) or both directions (bidirect=
ional, in a dual ring).

Each device acts as a repeater =E2=80=94 it receives data from one neighbor=
 and forwards it to the next until it reaches its destination.

Number of Links

