<hr data-start=3D"153" data-end=3D"156">
<h2 data-start=3D"158" data-end=3D"171"><strong data-start=3D"161" data-end=
=3D"171">Q2 (a)</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"172" data-end=3D"290"><strong data-start=3D"172" data-end=
=3D"185">Question:</strong><br data-start=3D"185" data-end=3D"188">
In a networking layer device, what is the purpose of having physical layer =
and data link layer? (5M)</p>
<p data-start=3D"292" data-end=3D"305"><strong data-start=3D"292" data-end=
=3D"303">Answer:</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"306" data-end=3D"818">
<li data-start=3D"306" data-end=3D"570">
<p data-start=3D"308" data-end=3D"429">The <strong data-start=3D"312" data-=
end=3D"330">Physical Layer</strong> ensures the <strong data-start=3D"343" =
data-end=3D"378">actual transmission of raw bits</strong> over the physical=
 medium (cables, Wi-Fi, fiber).</p>
<ul data-start=3D"433" data-end=3D"570">
<li data-start=3D"433" data-end=3D"521">
<p data-start=3D"435" data-end=3D"521">It deals with voltage levels, modula=
tion, transmission rate, connectors, pin layout.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"525" data-end=3D"570">
<p data-start=3D"527" data-end=3D"570">Without it, data cannot leave the de=
vice.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"572" data-end=3D"818">
<p data-start=3D"574" data-end=3D"697">The <strong data-start=3D"578" data-=
end=3D"597">Data Link Layer</strong> ensures that the raw transmission is <=
strong data-start=3D"635" data-end=3D"660">organized into frames</strong> a=
nd free from errors due to noise.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"701" data-end=3D"818">
<li data-start=3D"701" data-end=3D"771">
<p data-start=3D"703" data-end=3D"771">It provides <strong data-start=3D"71=
5" data-end=3D"768">error detection, flow control, and MAC addressing</stro=
ng>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"775" data-end=3D"818">
<p data-start=3D"777" data-end=3D"818">Ensures reliable node-to-node delive=
ry.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"820" data-end=3D"834">=F0=9F=91=89 Together:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"835" data-end=3D"1059">
<li data-start=3D"835" data-end=3D"888">
<p data-start=3D"837" data-end=3D"888">Physical layer provides the <strong =
data-start=3D"865" data-end=3D"885">hardware channel</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"889" data-end=3D"962">
<p data-start=3D"891" data-end=3D"962">Data Link ensures the <strong data-s=
tart=3D"913" data-end=3D"959">reliable and efficient use of that channel</s=
trong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"963" data-end=3D"1059">
<p data-start=3D"965" data-end=3D"1059">Example: In Ethernet =E2=86=92 Phys=
ical =3D cable &amp; signals; Data Link =3D MAC addressing + error check.</=
p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1061" data-end=3D"1064">
<h2 data-start=3D"1066" data-end=3D"1081"><strong data-start=3D"1069" data-=
