<p data-start=3D"1082" data-end=3D"1289"><strong data-start=3D"1082" data-e=
nd=3D"1095">Question:</strong><br data-start=3D"1095" data-end=3D"1098">
Explain the scenario of whether the segment encapsulates frames or frames e=
ncapsulate segments. How is error control at transport layer different from=
 error control at data link layer? (5M)</p>
<p data-start=3D"1291" data-end=3D"1304"><strong data-start=3D"1291" data-e=
nd=3D"1302">Answer:</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1305" data-end=3D"2055">
<li data-start=3D"1305" data-end=3D"1541">
<p data-start=3D"1307" data-end=3D"1327"><strong data-start=3D"1307" data-e=
nd=3D"1325">Encapsulation:</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1331" data-end=3D"1541">
<li data-start=3D"1331" data-end=3D"1382">
<p data-start=3D"1333" data-end=3D"1382">Data unit at <strong data-start=3D=
"1346" data-end=3D"1365">Transport Layer</strong> =3D <strong data-start=3D=
"1368" data-end=3D"1379">Segment</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1386" data-end=3D"1470">
<p data-start=3D"1388" data-end=3D"1470">At the sender, each <strong data-s=
tart=3D"1408" data-end=3D"1444">segment is placed inside a frame</strong> b=
y the Data Link Layer.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1474" data-end=3D"1541">
<p data-start=3D"1476" data-end=3D"1541">Therefore: <strong data-start=3D"1=
487" data-end=3D"1518">Frames encapsulate Segments</strong> (not the other =
way).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1543" data-end=3D"2055">
<p data-start=3D"1545" data-end=3D"1576"><strong data-start=3D"1545" data-e=
nd=3D"1574">Error Control Difference:</strong></p>
<ol data-start=3D"1580" data-end=3D"2055">
<li data-start=3D"1580" data-end=3D"1790">
<p data-start=3D"1583" data-end=3D"1605"><strong data-start=3D"1583" data-e=
nd=3D"1603">Data Link Layer:</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1612" data-end=3D"1790">
<li data-start=3D"1612" data-end=3D"1698">
<p data-start=3D"1614" data-end=3D"1698">Ensures <strong data-start=3D"1622=
" data-end=3D"1682">error-free delivery between two directly connected node=
s</strong> (hop-to-hop).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1705" data-end=3D"1752">
<p data-start=3D"1707" data-end=3D"1752">Uses CRC, ARQ, ACK/NACK for retran=
smission.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1759" data-end=3D"1790">
<p data-start=3D"1761" data-end=3D"1790">Works only within one link.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1795" data-end=3D"2055">
<p data-start=3D"1798" data-end=3D"1820"><strong data-start=3D"1798" data-e=
nd=3D"1818">Transport Layer:</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1827" data-end=3D"2055">
<li data-start=3D"1827" data-end=3D"1907">
<p data-start=3D"1829" data-end=3D"1907">Ensures <strong data-start=3D"1837=
" data-end=3D"1865">end-to-end error control</strong> (from source host to =
destination host).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1914" data-end=3D"1974">
<p data-start=3D"1916" data-end=3D"1974">Uses checksums, sequence numbers, =
ACKs, retransmissions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1981" data-end=3D"2055">
<p data-start=3D"1983" data-end=3D"2055">Responsible for reliability of ent=
ire session, not just a single link.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2057" data-end=3D"2187">=F0=9F=91=89 So:<br data-start=3D"=
2063" data-end=3D"2066">
<strong data-start=3D"2066" data-end=3D"2098">Frame =3D container of segmen=
t</strong>, and <strong data-start=3D"2104" data-end=3D"2147">error control=
 at transport =3D end-to-end</strong>, while at <strong data-start=3D"2158"=
 data-end=3D"2184">data link =3D hop-to-hop</strong>.</p>
